title: Click Landmarks
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
modified: 20260804100345811

Following a link records a landmark: which tiddler you were in, where the link sits inside that tiddler, and where it sat on your screen at the moment you clicked.

If you reached this tiddler through the link in [[Scroll Memory Documentation]], a floating button is showing at the bottom right of the window right now. Click it: you get back the exact view you had when you clicked, and the link blinks three times so you spot it immediately.

By default only long tiddlers record landmarks, because short ones have nothing to lose. The [[always active mode|Back and Forward Buttons]] extends recording to every click in the story river. Landmarks survive closing their tiddler; see [[Automatic Restore on Close]] for what happens then.
